---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Tools · borck.consulting" description="Free tools for briefing AI, keeping your voice, deciding like you, and checking the output.">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Tools</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title">Free tools for working with AI.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      A small suite for finding the first move, briefing AI, keeping your voice,
      deciding like you, and checking the output. No login. No tracking. Your work
      stays in your browser.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-sub" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      The tools are steps in <a href="/method">the method</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">Available now</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-grid">
      <a class="tier-card" href="/tools/rtcf/" style="text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Brief</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Brief Like You</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          The RTCF brief builder. Brief AI the way you would brief a capable
          colleague: context, constraints, and the check.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="tier-card" href="/tools/talk-like-you/" style="text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Voice</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Talk Like You</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Build a voice brief from your own writing, test it blind, and reuse the
          prompt. Your voice, not a generic assistant.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="tier-card" href="/tools/first-move-canvas/" style="text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Workshop</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">First Move Canvas</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Find one AI move worth making, assign every step, and set the 30-day
          gate before the pilot. Built for a meeting or a workshop.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a class="tier-card" href="https://trusttool.borck.education" style="text-decoration: none;">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Check</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">The Trust Tool</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Sort AI tasks by consequence and precision. A ten-second habit for
          deciding how much scrutiny an output needs.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-title">In development</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tier-grid">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-card-eyebrow">Decide</div>
        <div class="tier-card-title">Decide Like You</div>
        <p class="tier-card-desc">
          Capture one repeated decision, turn it into if-then rules, and test it
          blind. The method is adapted from Dylan Davis, Decide Like Me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="scope-line">
    The suite: find the first move, brief it, sound like you, decide like you, check it.
  </p>

</Base>
